<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#woodblock-printing">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Woodblock printing</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as wood-block printing</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Woodblock <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> is a technique of printing text or images by carving them in relief on a wooden block, inking it and pressing paper onto it. It developed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and was in use under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a>, which produced some of the earliest surviving printed texts, including the Diamond Sutra of 868. Accounts of the Tang Dynasty treat printing as one of the period's significant technological developments.</p></div>
